Spot the alternate segment for a given tangent and chord
Find missing angles using the theorem together with angles on a straight line and in a triangle', 'Circle theorems, Tangents and chords, Inscribed angles, Angle chasing, Geometric reasoning', 'The angle between a tangent and a chord at the point of contact is equal to the angle in the alternate segment.', 'The tangent PQ touches the circle at A. The chord AB cuts the circle into two segments. The angle between AQ and AB equals angle ACB, where C is any point on the arc on the other side of the chord. Why: angle ACB is an inscribed angle, so it is half the arc AB. The tangent-chord angle at A is also half the arc AB, because a tangent is the limit of a chord through A. Two halves of the same arc are equal.', 8, 'Polygons: circle theorems', 'Form 4', 'Calculate angles using circle theorems, including the angle in the alternate segment and the tangent and radius.', '', 'assets/figures/segment-theorem.svg', '', '', '', '', '', false)
